      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T13:38:30Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(edm): wire taper by angle word - the control's corner rule as machine data\n\nA wire EDM may state an angle-word taper dialect (edm.taper_angle: the\nside a positive angle leans the top, and the corner rule mitre or cone,\neach enumerated with no default) with edm.codes.taper_angle ({angle}).\nThe generator lays what the stated rule cuts - mitre is #536's path\nbyte for byte, cone pivots the wire about each top corner with its lean\nheld - so the wire laws judge the real lean and a corner the rule\ngouges blocks the post. The post writes taper_on and the signed angle\nword before the lead-in, X Y on the programmed (top) plane, no U/V, and\ntaper_off before the lead-out. An unstated rule, a machine stating\nneither uv nor an angle word, and a 4-axis cut on an angle-word machine\nare refused by name. U/V machines are byte-identical.\n\nFixes #1164\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
