        "date": "2026-11-13T19:50:41Z"
      },
      "message": "Merge main into issue/1164-wire-taper-angle-word (wire_op.rs, posting_wire.rs, wire_edm/mod.rs, wire_edm/taper.rs, machine/edm.rs, machine/mod.rs: both sides kept)\n\nMain brought #1181 (4-axis), #539 tabs, #540 burnout and #1109 open\nruns into the wire code; this branch adds the #1164 angle-word dialect.\n\n- posting_wire.rs: main's per-section post (tab cut-off) kept; the\n  lean is now Lean::Guides (U/V) or Lean::Angle, chosen once in\n  stream() with the PR's refusals (4-axis on an angle machine,\n  incomplete dialect, unresolved top) and applied per section.\n- wire_op.rs: main's burnout clearance door, cutoff condition and\n  4-axis refusals kept; the corner rule is read before the 4-axis\n  branch, so a 4-axis cut on an angle-word machine is still refused.\n- machine/edm.rs: main's strict key list kept; taper_angle added to\n  WIRE_KEYS, parsed after the orbits (main parses conditions earlier).\n- machine/mod.rs, wire_edm/mod.rs, taper.rs: both sides' exports and\n  docs kept.\n- open_tests.rs, posted_gates/wire.rs (main's): WireTaper literals\n  state corner: WireCorner::Mitre.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
